    {
      "@id": "sce:d",
      "@type": "urpx:RatePlan",
      "urpx:hasRatePlanVersion": {
        "@id": "sce:d-2026-03-20"
      },
      "urpx:initialEffectiveDate": "1949-08-01",
      "urpx:name": "Schedule D Domestic Service",
      "urpx:ratePlanUniqueIdentifier": "D",
      "urpx:timezoneIdentifier": "America/Los_Angeles"
    },
    {
      "@id": "sce:d-2026-03-20",
      "@type": "urpx:RatePlanVersion",
      "urpx:changeReason": {
        "@id": "urpx:rateCase"
      },
      "urpx:commodity": {
        "@id": "urpx:electricity"
      },
      "urpx:customerChoice": {
        "@id": "urpx:voluntaryChoice"
      },
      "urpx:description": "Tiered residential schedule (no time-of-use). Generation, distribution, and most flat-rate surcharges do not vary by tier or season. The two-tier structure (baseline / nonbaseline) is implemented via the Conservation Incentive Adjustment (CIA): customers receive a CIA credit of $-0.03740/kWh for usage at-or-below their daily baseline allocation, and pay a CIA charge of $+0.06368/kWh for usage above. The 10.108¢ swing matches the Baseline Credit modeled in SCE TOU-D options. Baseline allocations vary by Baseline Region (5/6/8/9/10/13/14/15/16), season (Summer = June-September; Winter = October-May), and whether the customer's primary heat source is electric (Basic vs All-Electric) per Preliminary Statement Part H. Schedule D is the legacy default destination for residential customers who opt out of the CPUC TOU mass-migration default schedules (TOU-D-4-9PM, TOU-D-5-8PM); enrollment is declining as opt-outs migrate to TOU over time. Replaces the prior Basic Charge + Minimum Charge structure with an income-graduated Base Services Charge (BSC) of $0.794/meter/day per Decision 24-05-028, with a Deed-Restricted discount of $(0.332)/meter/day. CARE/FERA discounts (32.5% and 18% respectively) and the related BSC surcharge exemption + BSC discount adjustments are documented in Special Conditions and modeled separately as RatePlanModifiers at ca/iou/sce/care/ and ca/iou/sce/fera/; the Deed-Restricted discount referenced above is modeled at ca/iou/sce/deed-restricted/.",
      "urpx:effectiveDateTime": "2026-03-20T00:00:00",
      "urpx:forRatePlan": {
        "@id": "sce:d"
      },
      "urpx:hasCoverageClaim": {
        "@id": "sce:cc-d-2026-03-20"
      },
      "urpx:hasDataSourceReference": {
        "@id": "_:b0"
      },
